        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Both home chords, "
        },
        {
          "text": "A",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", are sitting in "
        },
        {
          "text": "Chord Shapes",
          "link": {
            "kind": "screen",
            "href": "/chord-shapes"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " whenever you want to hold one down and try a dial for yourself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The families explain why one home is major and the other minor. They don't yet explain why a mode leaning on its home sounds different from one floating above it — for that, you need to see exactly where the half steps fall."
        }
      ]
